; Field dressing satchel: a canvas bag with a painted cross on the flap.
; Carried rather than aimed, so no sights and no muzzle.
;
; The cross is the one white thing anybody carries, and deliberately so -- it is
; what tells a man across a field that the soldier walking toward his body is
; coming to pick him up rather than to finish him off.
